@startuml
title Diagrama de secuencia — Compra, recepción e inventario

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "ENCARGADO / COCINA / ADMINISTRADOR" as User
participant "Frontend web" as Frontend
participant "Purchases API" as Api
participant "Application\n(Purchases / Inventory)" as App
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Registro de compra ==

User -> Frontend : registrar compra
Frontend -> Api : POST /purchases
Api -> App : CreatePurchase(command)
App -> DB : guardar Purchase(PENDIENTE)\n+ PurchaseItems
App --> Api : compra registrada
Api --> Frontend : 201 Created
Frontend --> User : mostrar compra pendiente

note right of DB
Una compra PENDIENTE no incrementa inventario.
end note

== Recepción de compra ==

User -> Frontend : registrar recepción
Frontend -> Api : POST /purchase-receipts
Api -> App : ReceivePurchase(command)
App -> DB : obtener Purchase + Items

alt recepción aceptada
  App -> DB : guardar PurchaseReceipt\n(+ líneas si aplica)
  App -> DB : actualizar Purchase=RECIBIDA
  App -> DB : registrar InventoryMovements\n(entradas por compra)
  App -> DB : actualizar InventoryBalances
  App --> Api : compra recibida
  Api --> Frontend : 201 Created
  Frontend --> User : mostrar compra recibida
else recepción no aceptada
  App --> Api : no cambia inventario
  Api --> Frontend : 409/validación
  Frontend --> User : informar incidencia
end

== Cancelación antes de recepción ==

opt cancelar compra pendiente
  User -> Frontend : cancelar compra
  Frontend -> Api : PATCH /purchases/{id}/cancel
  Api -> App : CancelPurchase(command)
  App -> DB : actualizar Purchase=CANCELADA
  App --> Api : compra cancelada
  Api --> Frontend : 200 OK
  Frontend --> User : mostrar compra cancelada
end

note across
Solo el estado RECIBIDA incrementa inventario.
La baseline actual no modela recepción parcial estructurada.
end note

@enduml
